  user_input {
    user_response: "Build me an app with screens that look like this. You can hotlink images from the HTMLFINAL UX + UI REFINEMENT PASS FOR NEXORA\n\nDo NOT redesign the website from scratch.\n\nKeep the existing Nexora visual identity, layout, lavender + black + purple color system, typography, hero composition and overall art direction.\n\nYour job now is to make the website feel like a REAL, POLISHED, USER-FRIENDLY PRODUCT rather than an AI-generated prototype.\n\nThink like a senior product designer and frontend engineer.\n\n==================================================\n1. SIMPLIFY THE USER JOURNEY\n==================================================\n\nA new student should understand Nexora within 5 seconds.\n\nThe main journey should be:\n\nDiscover opportunity\n\342\206\222 Check eligibility\n\342\206\222 Prepare\n\342\206\222 Apply\n\342\206\222 Track result\n\342\206\222 Learn from rejection\n\nMake this flow obvious throughout the website.\n\nDo not overwhelm users with information.\n\nEvery screen should have ONE clear primary action.\n\n==================================================\n2. NAVIGATION\n==================================================\n\nKeep navigation minimal and predictable.\n\nUse:\n\nOpportunities\nPrepare\nProgress\n\nRight side:\n\nSign in\nGet started\n\nMake the active page visually obvious.\n\nOn mobile use a clean hamburger/menu.\n\nNavbar should remain visible when useful, but never take too much screen space.\n\n==================================================\n3. HOMEPAGE\n==================================================\n\nKeep the current hero exactly as the main visual statement.\n\nImprove the information hierarchy.\n\nThe user should immediately understand:\n\nWHAT:\nPlacement opportunities\n\nWHO:\nFreshers/students\n\nWHY:\nFind suitable jobs and prepare better\n\nACTION:\nFind my matches\n\nDo not add unnecessary text.\n\n==================================================\n4. OPPORTUNITY FEED\n==================================================\n\nMake the opportunity feed extremely easy to scan.\n\nEvery job card should have this hierarchy:\n\nCompany\n\342\206\223\nJob title\n\342\206\223\nMatch percentage\n\342\206\223\nEligibility\n\342\206\223\nDeadline\n\342\206\223\nImportant requirements\n\342\206\223\nPrimary action\n\nDo not make every piece of information equally prominent.\n\nUse visual hierarchy.\n\nExample:\n\n94% MATCH\n\n\342\234\223 ELIGIBLE\n\nSoftware Engineer Intern\n\nMicrosoft\n\nCloses in 3 days\n\nPython \302\267 DSA \302\267 SQL\n\n[View opportunity \342\206\222]\n\n==================================================\n5. MATCH SCORE\n==================================================\n\nMake the match score immediately understandable.\n\nUse a circular progress ring.\n\nExample:\n\n94%\nMATCH\n\nAdd a small explanation when hovered/clicked:\n\n\"Based on your CGPA, branch, skills and job requirements.\"\n\nDo not make users guess what the percentage means.\n\n==================================================\n6. ELIGIBILITY\n==================================================\n\nEligibility must NEVER be ambiguous.\n\nUse:\n\n\342\234\223 Eligible\n\342\232\240 Borderline\n\342\234\225 Not eligible\n\nWhen not eligible, immediately explain why.\n\nExample:\n\n\342\234\225 Not eligible\n\n\"Minimum CGPA: 8.0\nYour CGPA: 7.4\"\n\nDo not hide this information inside another page.\n\n==================================================\n7. PLACEMENT INBOX\n==================================================\n\nMake this feature extremely simple.\n\nThe user should understand it immediately:\n\nPASTE NOTICE\n\342\206\223\nAI EXTRACTS DETAILS\n\342\206\223\nCHECKS ELIGIBILITY\n\342\206\223\nCREATES OPPORTUNITY\n\nUse a large, comfortable input area.\n\nAfter processing, show a clean preview before saving.\n\nInclude:\n\nCompany\nRole\nSalary\nDeadline\nEligibility\nRounds\n\nAdd:\n\n[Save opportunity]\n\n==================================================\n8. RESUME GRILL\n==================================================\n\nDo not make it look like a generic chatbot.\n\nThe user journey should be:\n\nSelect job\n\342\206\222 Upload resume\n\342\206\222 See 3 biggest gaps\n\342\206\222 Start interview\n\nKeep the interface focused.\n\nShow the 3 most important gaps first.\n\nThen show:\n\n\"Questions an interviewer is likely to ask you\"\n\nThis should feel like a personal interview preparation tool.\n\n==================================================\n9. REJECTION AUTOPSY\n==================================================\n\nMake this feature emotionally friendly.\n\nDo NOT make rejection feel negative or punishing.\n\nInstead of overwhelming charts, show one clear insight.\n\nExample:\n\nYOUR BIGGEST PATTERN\n\n\"3 of your last 4 rejections happened during aptitude.\"\n\nThen:\n\nWHAT TO DO NEXT\n\n\"Practice 20 aptitude questions before your next assessment.\"\n\nUse a simple visual trend underneath.\n\n==================================================\n10. PROGRESS PAGE\n==================================================\n\nKeep it simple.\n\nShow:\n\nApplications\nInterviews\nOffers\nRejections\n\nThen immediately show:\n\nYOUR NEXT FOCUS\n\n\"Aptitude is currently your biggest improvement area.\"\n\nAvoid creating a complicated analytics dashboard.\n\n==================================================\n11. MICROCOPY\n\nReplace generic AI-generated copy with short, human copy.\n\nAvoid:\n\n\"Unlock your potential\"\n\"Empower your career\"\n\"AI-powered career transformation\"\n\"Revolutionize your placement journey\"\n\nUse:\n\n\"Find jobs you actually qualify for.\"\n\n\"Know why you matched.\"\n\n\"Prepare for this job.\"\n\n\"Learn from the rejection.\"\n\nUse plain language that Indian college students naturally understand.\n\n==================================================\n12. LOADING STATES\n==================================================\n\nNever show a blank screen.\n\nWhen AI is processing:\n\nReading notice...\nFinding requirements...\nChecking eligibility...\nBuilding your match...\n\nUse skeleton loaders for feeds.\n\n==================================================\n13. EMPTY STATES\n==================================================\n\nEvery empty state should tell the user:\n\nWHAT happened\n+\nWHAT to do next\n\nExample:\n\n\"No opportunities yet.\"\n\n\"Paste your first placement notice to get started.\"\n\n[Add opportunity]\n\n==================================================\n14. ERROR STATES\n==================================================\n\nNever show technical errors like:\n\n\"Something went wrong.\"\n\nInstead:\n\n\"We couldn\'t read that notice.\"\n\n\"Try pasting the original placement message again.\"\n\n[Try again]\n\nMake errors useful.\n\n==================================================\n15. FORMS\n==================================================\n\nEvery input must have:\n\n- clear label\n- example/placeholder\n- validation\n- helpful error message\n\nDo not rely only on placeholder text.\n\nKeep forms short.\n\nUse sensible defaults.\n\n==================================================\n16. RESPONSIVENESS\n==================================================\n\nPerform a complete mobile-first refinement.\n\nCheck:\n\n320px\n375px\n390px\n768px\n1024px\n1440px\n\nNothing should overflow horizontally.\n\nCards should stack naturally.\n\nButtons should remain easy to tap.\n\nText should remain readable.\n\nHero should remain visually impressive on mobile.\n\n==================================================\n17. ACCESSIBILITY\n==================================================\n\nEnsure:\n\nWCAG AA contrast\n\nKeyboard navigation\n\nVisible focus states\n\nAccessible buttons\n\nAccessible form labels\n\nLogical tab order\n\nNo interaction should depend only on hover.\n\nImportant information must also be visible on mobile/touch devices.\n\n==================================================\n18. INTERACTIONS\n==================================================\n\nKeep the existing cursor-following glow.\n\nRefine it so it is:\n\nsubtle\nsmooth\nresponsive\nnot distracting\n\nAdd:\n\ncard hover lift\nbutton press feedback\nsmooth filter transitions\nmatch ring animation\npage transitions\n\nUse motion sparingly.\n\nThe interface should feel fast.\n\n==================================================\n19. VISUAL CONSISTENCY\n==================================================\n\nCreate one consistent design system.\n\nStandardize:\n\nborder radius\nspacing\nbutton heights\ncard padding\nheading sizes\nbody text\nicon sizes\ninput styles\nstatus badges\n\nDo not let every component have a different style.\n\n==================================================\n20. PERFORMANCE\n==================================================\n\nKeep the website fast.\n\nAvoid unnecessary:\n\nlarge images\nheavy animations\nduplicate components\nunnecessary libraries\n\nAnimations should not block interaction.\n\n==================================================\n21. FINAL \"HUMAN DESIGN\" PASS\n==================================================\n\nLook through every page and ask:\n\n\"Would a real student understand this immediately?\"\n\n\"Is there anything unnecessary?\"\n\n\"Is the next action obvious?\"\n\n\"Does anything look like an AI-generated template?\"\n\nRemove anything that feels decorative without purpose.\n\nPrioritize usability over adding more features.\n\n==================================================\nFINAL RULE\n==================================================\n\nDO NOT ADD NEW FEATURES.\n\nDO NOT REDESIGN THE CURRENT VISUAL STYLE.\n\nDO NOT CHANGE THE CORE 4 MODULES.\n\nDO NOT CHANGE THE LAVENDER + BLACK + PURPLE IDENTITY.\n\nONLY:\n\nREFINE\nSIMPLIFY\nIMPROVE UX\nIMPROVE RESPONSIVENESS\nIMPROVE ACCESSIBILITY\nIMPROVE MICRO-INTERACTIONS\nIMPROVE COPY\nREMOVE UNNECESSARY UI\n\nThe final product should feel like:\n\n\"Someone spent weeks polishing this product\"\n\n\342\200\224not\342\200\224\n\n\"AI generated a website in one prompt.\""
    items {
      text: "Build me an app with screens that look like this. You can hotlink images from the HTMLFINAL UX + UI REFINEMENT PASS FOR NEXORA\n\nDo NOT redesign the website from scratch.\n\nKeep the existing Nexora visual identity, layout, lavender + black + purple color system, typography, hero composition and overall art direction.\n\nYour job now is to make the website feel like a REAL, POLISHED, USER-FRIENDLY PRODUCT rather than an AI-generated prototype.\n\nThink like a senior product designer and frontend engineer.\n\n==================================================\n1. SIMPLIFY THE USER JOURNEY\n==================================================\n\nA new student should understand Nexora within 5 seconds.\n\nThe main journey should be:\n\nDiscover opportunity\n\342\206\222 Check eligibility\n\342\206\222 Prepare\n\342\206\222 Apply\n\342\206\222 Track result\n\342\206\222 Learn from rejection\n\nMake this flow obvious throughout the website.\n\nDo not overwhelm users with information.\n\nEvery screen should have ONE clear primary action.\n\n==================================================\n2. NAVIGATION\n==================================================\n\nKeep navigation minimal and predictable.\n\nUse:\n\nOpportunities\nPrepare\nProgress\n\nRight side:\n\nSign in\nGet started\n\nMake the active page visually obvious.\n\nOn mobile use a clean hamburger/menu.\n\nNavbar should remain visible when useful, but never take too much screen space.\n\n==================================================\n3. HOMEPAGE\n==================================================\n\nKeep the current hero exactly as the main visual statement.\n\nImprove the information hierarchy.\n\nThe user should immediately understand:\n\nWHAT:\nPlacement opportunities\n\nWHO:\nFreshers/students\n\nWHY:\nFind suitable jobs and prepare better\n\nACTION:\nFind my matches\n\nDo not add unnecessary text.\n\n==================================================\n4. OPPORTUNITY FEED\n===================