  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Inspecting Initial Files**\n\nI\'ve begun by examining `src/App.tsx` and `index.html`, and am now listing the directory contents to get a handle on the initial file structure. I\'ve noted that `App.tsx` currently returns an empty `div`. My goal is to map out the entire project before digging in deeper. I am currently inspecting all `src/` files.\n\n\n**Analyzing Project Data**\n\nI\'ve determined that the `src` directory holds only `App.tsx`, `index.css`, and `main.tsx`. Now, I am carefully reviewing the user\'s request and associated theme prompt. I\'m focusing on the color definitions to ensure I understand how the styles should be integrated, before I get started. I have also noted the absence of any other directories.\n\n\n**Defining Color Values**\n\nI\'ve extracted the color definitions, noting the specific hex codes for error states, fixed primary, secondary, and tertiary colors, background, and surface variants. I also have the typography including fonts like `DM Sans`, `DM Serif Display`, and `JetBrains Mono`, and am preparing to implement the design system. The user\'s prompt emphasizes preserving the existing Nexora visual identity.\n\n\n**Refining User Experience**\n\nI\'m now focusing on user journey simplification, aiming for immediate Nexora understanding. The primary flow \342\200\223 Discover, Check, Prepare, Apply, Track, Learn \342\200\223 is being prioritized for clear website navigation. The goal is to emphasize a single, clear action per screen. Navigation will be minimal with predictable options: Opportunities, Prepare, Progress, Sign In, Get Started. I\'m focusing on the clarity of the active page and a mobile-friendly navbar.\n\n\n**Prioritizing User Clarity**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the user\'s initial experience. The hero section must remain as is, but I\'m restructuring the information to make it immediately clear what opportunities are, who they\'re for, and why they should care, with a clear call to action. I want to minimize text and maximize impact. I am prioritizing a very scannable opportunity feed with a consistent information hierarchy. I will use visual hierarchy to make the match score easily understandable.\n\n\n**Clarifying User Feedback**\n\nI\'m now integrating crucial feedback regarding progress indicators and eligibility displays. I\'m focusing on a clear, non-ambiguous display for the match percentage, providing an explanation upon hover. I\'m also ensuring the \"Eligible\" status uses clear icons (checkmark, warning, x) with immediate explanations for ineligibility, avoiding any hidden information. I\'m keeping the in-box feature simple, with paste-to-opportunity creation as the central design concept. I will be sure to add the elements that I noted from the existing project.\n\n\n**Designing Feature Updates**\n\nI\'m now outlining key feature enhancements. For \"Resume Grill,\" I\'m focusing on a streamlined user journey: job selection, resume upload, and immediate display of the top three skill gaps, followed by interview preparation questions. The interface will be concise and feel personal. For \"Rejection Autopsy,\" I want to create a positive experience, focusing on one key insight per rejection, paired with a clear, actionable recommendation. A simple visual trend will support the insight. The \"Progress Page\" will be kept clean, displaying essential application data.\n\n\n**Crafting Actionable Insights**\n\nI\'m now integrating feedback regarding interview, offer, and rejection tracking. I\'m focusing on providing users with immediately actionable insights, like identifying their biggest improvement area. Avoiding complex dashboards is paramount. My focus is on crafting concise, helpful guidance.\n\n\\n\\n\n\n**Simplifying Microcopy**\n\nI\'m now replacing generic AI-generated copy with concise, human-friendly alternatives. I\'m using straightforward language that resonates with Indian college students. I\'m aiming for clarity and relatability, ensuring users understand the value proposition effortlessly.\n\n\\n\\n\n\n**Designing Loading & Empty States**\n\nI am now focusing on loading states and empty states, ensuring a smooth user experience. I am replacing blank screens with informative prompts during AI processing. For instance, I am including messages such as, \"Reading notice...\" and \"Checking eligibility...\" when appropriate. I will be incorporating skeleton loaders for the feeds. I also plan to make use of clear explanations in all empty states to guide users.\n\n\n**Refining Error Handling**\n\nI\'m now focusing on error states. I will never display technical errors, and instead offer user-friendly, actionable messages like \"We couldn\'t read that notice\" or \"Try pasting the original placement message again.\" Clear labels, placeholders, validation, and sensible defaults will be crucial for all forms.\n\n\n**Ensuring Visual Integrity**\n\nI\'m now carefully implementing the specified color palette and design system to guarantee visual consistency. I\'m focusing on the interplay of muted lavender, dark containers, and crisp typography to maintain Nexora\'s brand identity. I\'m also planning my strategy for the required performance, aiming for a swift user experience without any blocking.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
