    thinking: "**Exploring CSS Configuration**\n\nI\'m currently investigating how to leverage CSS utilities and theme variables within `src/index.css` using `@import \"tailwindcss\";`. Specifically, I\'m focusing on defining a custom theme with `@theme`, similar to Tailwind CSS v4\'s implementation. This includes exploring how to set variables such as `--font-sans` for a specific font.\n\n\n**Refining Visual Feedback**\n\nI\'m now focusing on refining the visual feedback elements. I\'m prioritizing subtle animations for hover effects and button presses to enhance the user experience. I\'m also considering smooth filter transitions and matching ring animations to create a more polished feel. The goal is to make the interface feel fast and responsive without being distracting, and to match existing design patterns where applicable.\n\n\n**Prioritizing User Flow**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the user flow, aiming for clarity. I want to make the \"Track result \342\206\222 Learn from rejection\" loop obvious throughout the site. Avoiding information overload is key; each screen must have one primary action. Navigation will be minimal and predictable, using \"Opportunities,\" \"Prepare,\" and \"Progress.\" The homepage will keep its hero visual, but I\342\200\231m reworking the information hierarchy to quickly convey what, who, why, and the action to take. I\'m streamlining the opportunity feed for easy scanning with a clearly defined information hierarchy on job cards.\n\n\n**Clarifying Information Presentation**\n\nI\'m now completely focused on making crucial information immediately clear. Specifically, I\342\200\231m working on presenting match scores visually using circular progress rings, with hover explanations to eliminate ambiguity. Eligibility status will be unambiguous with clear symbols (\342\234\223, \342\232\240, \342\234\225) and immediate explanations for ineligibility. For the placement inbox, I want to streamline the process: it will be a simple \"paste, extract, check, and create\" flow, with a preview before saving.\n\n\n**Refining User Journey**\n\nI\'m now prioritizing the user journey: select job, upload resume, and identify the top three gaps. I want the interface streamlined to focus on immediate needs, not on overwhelming users. I\'m focusing on \"Questions an interviewer is likely to ask you\" based on the uploaded resume and identified gaps. My goal is to craft a personal interview prep tool.\n\n\\n\\n\n\n**Streamlining Rejection Analysis**\n\nI\'ve shifted focus to the \"Rejection Autopsy\" feature, striving for a supportive tone. Instead of complex charts, I\'ll provide a single, actionable insight like \"YOUR BIGGEST PATTERN: 3 of your last 4 rejections happened during aptitude.\" I\'ll immediately follow this with \"WHAT TO DO NEXT: Practice 20 aptitude questions before your next assessment,\" with a simple visual trend for context. The goal is to make it encouraging.\n\n\n\n**Defining User Interactions**\n\nNow, I\'m focusing on defining core user actions and the language used. I plan to use phrases like \"Find jobs you actually qualify for,\" \"Know why you matched,\" \"Prepare for this job,\" and \"Learn from the rejection\" with plain language that\'s easily understood. I\'m also planning how to handle loading, empty, and error states, ensuring clear messaging, specific next steps, and helpful error guidance. Form design will include clear labels, examples, validations, and helpful error messages with defaults. I am prioritizing responsive design for multiple breakpoints and WCAG AA contrast for accessibility.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Accessibility**\n\nI\'m now prioritizing accessibility and user interactions, planning keyboard navigation with visible focus states, and creating accessible buttons and form labels, never hover-only. I\'m focusing on providing visual consistency with the brand spec, including a lavender canvas, obsidian blacks, and secondary purples. Typography includes DM Sans, DM Serif Display (italic nuances), and JetBrains Mono for data. I\'m also ensuring fast performance with zero layout shifts. I\'m streamlining the core four modules: Opportunities and Placement Inbox.\n\n\n**Refining Key Module Interactions**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on integrating the \'Save opportunity\' function directly into the feed for quick access. Following that, the focus is on the \"Resume Grill\" module, streamlining the process of selecting a job, uploading a resume (with automatic stats extraction like CGPA and skills), and immediate gap identification. This feeds into the \"Questions an interviewer is likely to ask you\" section. Finally, I\'m working to make the Progress section and Rejection Autopsy more data-rich yet emotionally accessible, summarizing key stats and providing actionable insights for growth. I\'m focusing on making the rejection information supportive rather than discouraging, and making adding more data easy.\n\n\n**Structuring Application Logic**\n\nI\'m now focused on structuring the application, setting up types for key entities like opportunities, match scores, and student profiles within `src/types.ts`. I\'m also preparing mock data within `src/data/mockData.ts` for realistic placement opportunities. Navigation will be streamlined using `Opportunities | Prepare | Progress` with a quick action button. I\'m checking `lucide-react` icons for available options.\n\n\n**Defining Mock Data**\n\nI\'m now focusing on defining mock data and user interface components. I\'m adding realistic placement opportunities from companies (e.g. Amazon, Deloitte) within an Indian campus placement context, including CTC, LPA, branches, CGPA criteria, and assessment types. I\'m creating a sample student profile (\"Aman Sharma\") and TPO notices for easy pasting. The navigation is minimal (Nexora, Opportunities, Prepare, Progress, Sign In / Profile). I am building a subtle cursor glow, a circular match ring, and EligibilityBadges.\n\n\n**Defining Eligibility Feedback**\n\nI\'m now prioritizing clear eligibility status feedback using concise visuals and text. I\'m designing components for `Eligible` (emerald with a lavender tint), `Borderline` (amber with purple tint), and `Not Eligible` states. Each \'Not Eligible\' status will provide an immediate inline breakdown, such as CGPA criteria differences. I\'m focusing on incorporating these indicators within the opportunity feed. I\'m also ensuring the HeroSection, JourneyFlow, and OpportunityFeed components are clearly designed and user-friendly. I will prioritize making all of these visual elements accessible and intuitive.\n\n\n**Refining Inbox Workflow**\n\nI\'m now streamlining the placement inbox. The primary action will be to view opportunities or prepare for a role. The detailed modal will include one-click options to \'Prepare in Resume Grill\' or \'Mark as Applied\'. The inbox will involve pasting notices, extracting details, checking eligibility, and then creating opportunities. I\'m focusing on a clean preview before saving and easy addition to the opportunity feed.\n\n\n**Developing Interview Insights**\n\nI\'m now prioritizing the \"Questions an interviewer is likely to ask you\" section. I want to build structured interview questions based on identified resume gaps. Specifically, the goal is to define key points to mention and create an interactive practice/feedback card. I\'m streamlining the progress page with high-clarity stats on applications, interviews, offers, and rejections. I\'m also ensuring a user-friendly rejection autopsy with actionable insights. I will also make the student profile modal dynamic.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_407911"
      name: "edit_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"Instruction\":\"Add font families, design tokens, and smooth glow effects to index.css\", \"ReplacementContent\":\"@import \\\"tailwindcss\\\";\\n\\n@layer base {\\n  :root {\\n    --font-sans: \'DM Sans\', system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif;\\n    --font-serif: \'DM Serif Display\', Georgia, serif;\\n    --font-mono: \'JetBrains Mono\', monospace;\\n  }\\n\\n  body {\\n    font-family: var(--font-sans);\\n    background-color: #fcf8ff;\\n    color: #1c1a28;\\n    overflow-x: hidden;\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n.font-serif-display {\\n  font-family: \'DM Serif Display\', Georgia, serif;\\n}\\n\\n.font-mono-code {\\n  font-family: \'JetBrains Mono\', monospace;\\n}\\n\\n/* Custom subtle cursor glow */\\n.cursor-glow-dot {\\n  pointer-events: none;\\n  position: fixed;\\n  width: 420px;\\n  height: 420px;\\n  border-radius: 50%;\\n  background: radial-gradient(circle, rgba(169, 161, 214, 0.22) 0%, rgba(199, 191, 234, 0.08) 45%, transparent 70%);\\n  transform: translate(-50%, -50%);\\n  transition: transform 0.12s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1), opacity 0.3s ease;\\n  z-index: 1;\\n}\\n\\n/* Card hover lift & press feedback */\\n.nexora-card-lift {\\n  transition: transform 0.18s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1), box-shadow 0.18s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1), border-color 0.18s ease;\\n}\\n\\n.nexora-card-lift:hover {\\n  transform: translateY(-2px);\\n}\\n\\n.nexora-btn-press {\\n  transition: transform 0.12s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1), opacity 0.12s ease;\\n}\\n\\n.nexora-btn-press:active {\\n  transform: scale(0.98);\\n}\\n\", \"TargetContent\":\"@import \\\"tailwindcss\\\";\\n\", \"TargetFile\":\"/src/index.css\", \"toolAction\":\"Enhancing index.css\", \"toolSummary\":\"Add typography, styles, and hover effects\"}"
      thought_signature: ""
      original_name: "edit_file"
