.\',\n      recommendation: \'Add a bullet acknowledging unit test coverage (e.g. \"Maintained 84% test coverage using pytest fixtures and GitHub Actions\").\',\n    },\n  ],\n};\n\nexport const sampleQuestionsForRole: Record<string, InterviewQuestion[]> = {\n  default: [\n    {\n      id: \'q-1\',\n      question: \'How does your FastAPI backend handle database connection pooling under high concurrent traffic?\',\n      category: \'Technical\',\n      whyAsked: \'Your resume features a FastAPI project as your primary highlight, but the job requires handling high-volume transactions.\',\n      keyPointsToCover: [\n        \'Mention SQLAlchemy async engine or asyncpg connection pool parameters (pool_size=20, max_overflow=10)\',\n        \'Explain how connection exhaustion leads to HTTP 500/504 errors if connections are not returned cleanly\',\n        \'State how you would implement Redis caching for read-heavy query patterns to reduce database pool pressure\',\n      ],\n    },\n    {\n      id: \'q-2\',\n      question: \'Given an array of transaction timestamps, how would you design an efficient sliding-window rate limiter?\',\n      category: \'DSA / System\',\n      whyAsked: \'Standard assessment pattern for payment and backend roles (Microsoft, Razorpay, PhonePe).\',\n      keyPointsToCover: [\n        \'Compare Fixed Window vs Sliding Window Log vs Token Bucket algorithm\',\n        \'Demonstrate O(log N) or O(1) time complexity using Redis Sorted Sets (ZADD, ZREMRANGEBYSCORE, ZCARD)\',\n        \'Address edge cases: race conditions during distributed concurrent requests using Lua scripts\',\n      ],\n    },\n    {\n      id: \'q-3\',\n      question: \'Tell me about a bug you encountered that took more than a day to resolve. What was your systematic debugging process?\',\n      category: \'Behavioral\',\n      whyAsked: \'Evaluates resilience, root-cause investigation rigor, and communication rather than surface-level answers.\',\n      keyPointsToCover: [\n        \'Frame using STAR method: Situation, Task, Action, Result\',\n        \'Do not blame third-party libraries without evidence; show how you isolated the variable using structured logging\',\n        \'Conclude with the preventative measure introduced (e.g. regression test or lint rule)\',\n      ],\n    },\n    {\n      id: \'q-4\',\n      question: \'In your React & Node project, how do you handle state reconciliation when client network drops midway through a submission?\',\n      category: \'Project Defense\',\n      whyAsked: \'Tests practical full-stack craftsmanship beyond basic tutorial boilerplate.\',\n      keyPointsToCover: [\n        \'Idempotency keys generated on client before network call\',\n        \'Optimistic UI state with rollback handler upon non-2xx status\',\n        \'Retry backoff policy with user-visible retry affordance\',\n      ],\n    },\n  ],\n};\n\nexport const initialRejections: RejectionRecord[] = [\n  {\n    id: \'rej-1\',\n    company: \'Swiggy\',\n    role: \'Software Engineer 1\',\n    stage: \'Aptitude / Online Test\',\n    date: \'Sep 28, 2026\',\n    primaryCause: \'Speed on quantitative aptitude (Probability and Time & Distance questions ran out of time).\',\n    takeaway: \'Coding score was 100%, but section cutoff for Quant was missed by 2 questions.\',\n  },\n  {\n    id: \'rej-2\',\n    company: \'Amazon\',\n    role: \'SDE Intern\',\n    stage: \'Aptitude / Online Test\',\n    date: \'Sep 19, 2026\',\n    primaryCause: \'Timed out during the 20-minute logical reasoning section of the HackerRank assessment.\',\n    takeaway: \'Aptitude time management is the bottleneck, not programming logic.\',\n  },\n  {\n    id: \'rej-3\',\n    company: \'CRED\',\n    role: \'Frontend Engineer Intern\',\n    stage: \'Technical Round 1\',\n    date: \'Sep 08, 2026\',\n    primaryCause: \'Hesitated when explaining React fiber architecture and concurrent mode reconciliation under the hood.\',\n    takeaway: \'Review core JavaScript event loop and React rendering lifecycle internals.\',\n  },\n  {\n    id: \'rej-4\',\n    company: \'TCS Digital\',\n    role: \'Systems Engineer\',\n    stage: \'Aptitude / Online Test\',\n    date: \'Aug 24, 2026\',\n    primaryCause: \'Advanced numerical ability section cutoff not cleared.\',\n    takeaway: \'Confirms the 3/4 recurring pattern across early-stage online tests.\',\n  },\n];\n\nexport const initialProgress: ProgressSummary = {\n  applications: 14,\n  interviews: 4,\n  offers: 1,\n  rejections: 5,\n  biggestPattern: {\n    headline: \'YOUR BIGGEST PATTERN\',\n    description: \'3 of your last 4 rejections happened during aptitude.\',\n    highlightCount: \'3 of 4 in Online Assessment\',\n  },\n  nextFocus: {\n    title: \'WHAT TO DO NEXT\',\n    action: \'Practice 20 aptitude questions before your next assessment.\',\n    suggestedDrill: \'Target Time & Work, Permutations, and Fast Mental Math (15 mins/day).\',\n  },\n};\n"
