  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Constructing Components**\n\nI\'m now focusing on building the components, starting with `MatchRing.tsx`. I intend to make the match score clear with a circular progress ring. This component needs to immediately convey the information in a simple, intuitive manner. I\'m prioritizing immediate understanding of the match score for the user.\n\n\n**Defining UI Elements**\n\nI\'ve been working on defining key UI elements. I\'ve got `MatchRing.tsx` underway, prioritizing clarity. My goal is for the match score to be instantly understandable. I am also working on `EligibilityBadge.tsx`, ensuring eligibility is never ambiguous with clear visual cues and immediate explanations. The cursor glow refinements are underway to be subtle, smooth, and responsive. Finally, I\'m defining a minimal and predictable navigation with a clear active page indicator for `Navbar.tsx`, and the existing `HeroSection.tsx` is staying as is.\n\n\n**Prioritizing User Flow**\n\nI\'m now simplifying the user journey for new students, aiming for instant understanding of Nexora. The flow will prioritize discovery, eligibility checks, preparation, application, tracking, and learning. I\'m focusing on making this process crystal clear across the website. I\'m also working on the OpportunityFeed\'s visual hierarchy, ensuring quick scanning. The key elements will be company, job title, match percentage, eligibility, deadline, key requirements, and primary action, with the match percentage and eligibility being most prominent.\n\n\n**Refining Opportunity Details**\n\nI\'m now focusing on refining the Opportunity Modal/Drawer, ensuring a clear primary action like \"Prepare for this job\" or \"Mark as Applied.\" I\'m also implementing skeleton loaders for feeds and empty states. Empty states will clearly communicate what happened and offer next steps. I\'m focusing on \"closes in 3 days\", as well as \"Python\", \"DSA\", and \"SQL\" tags, which must be clearly present. Finally, I\'m integrating a \"View opportunity\" button. I am also planning loading states for various actions.\n\n**Streamlining Placement Inbox**\n\nI\'m making `PlacementInbox.tsx` simple and intuitive. The goal is instant user understanding: Paste Notice \342\206\222 AI Extracts \342\206\222 Checks Eligibility \342\206\222 Creates Opportunity. I\'m incorporating a comfortable input area and a clean preview before saving. The details to include are Company, Role, Salary, Deadline, Eligibility, and Rounds. I\'m also adding a [Save opportunity] button. Loading states are also planned. Finally, there will be a sample notice button for immediate testing.\n\n**Focusing Resume Grill**\n\nI am now structuring the user journey for `ResumeGrill.tsx`. The goal is to avoid a generic chatbot interface. The flow should be: Select job \342\206\222 Upload resume \342\206\222 See details.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_499455"
      name: "create_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"Content\":\"import React, { useEffect, useState } from \'react\';\\n\\nexport const CursorGlow: React.FC = () => {\\n  const [position, setPosition] = useState({ x: -100, y: -100 });\\n  const [visible, setVisible] = useState(false);\\n\\n  useEffect(() => {\\n    // Disable on touch devices or if prefers-reduced-motion\\n    if (window.matchMedia(\'(pointer: coarse)\').matches) return;\\n    if (window.matchMedia(\'(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)\').matches) return;\\n\\n    let rafId: number;\\n    let targetX = -100;\\n    let targetY = -100;\\n    let currentX = -100;\\n    let currentY = -100;\\n\\n    const handleMouseMove = (e: MouseEvent) => {\\n      targetX = e.clientX;\\n      targetY = e.clientY;\\n      if (!visible) setVisible(true);\\n    };\\n\\n    const handleMouseLeave = () => {\\n      setVisible(false);\\n    };\\n\\n    const updatePosition = () => {\\n      // Smooth lerp interpolation for soft responsiveness\\n      currentX += (targetX - currentX) * 0.15;\\n      currentY += (targetY - currentY) * 0.15;\\n      setPosition({ x: currentX, y: currentY });\\n      rafId = requestAnimationFrame(updatePosition);\\n    };\\n\\n    window.addEventListener(\'mousemove\', handleMouseMove, { passive: true });\\n    document.addEventListener(\'mouseleave\', handleMouseLeave);\\n    rafId = requestAnimationFrame(updatePosition);\\n\\n    return () => {\\n      window.removeEventListener(\'mousemove\', handleMouseMove);\\n      document.removeEventListener(\'mouseleave\', handleMouseLeave);\\n      cancelAnimationFrame(rafId);\\n    };\\n  }, [visible]);\\n\\n  if (!visible) return null;\\n\\n  return (\\n    <div\\n      className=\\\"cursor-glow-dot\\\"\\n      style={{\\n        left: `${position.x}px`,\\n        top: `${position.y}px`,\\n        opacity: visible ? 1 : 0,\\n      }}\\n      aria-hidden=\\\"true\\\"\\n    />\\n  );\\n};\\n\", \"Overwrite\":true, \"TargetFile\":\"/src/components/CursorGlow.tsx\", \"toolAction\":\"Creating CursorGlow.tsx\", \"toolSummary\":\"Add subtle cursor glow\"}"
      thought_signature: ""
      original_name: "create_file"
    }
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 9
      nanos: 195652037
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
