  planner_response {
    response: "The UX and UI refinement pass for **Nexora** is complete, adhering to the lavender, black, and purple editorial identity:\n\n### What was refined\n\n- **Simplified User Journey**: The 6-stage campus placement loop (*Discover Opportunity \342\206\222 Check Eligibility \342\206\222 Prepare \342\206\222 Apply \342\206\222 Track Result \342\206\222 Learn from Rejection*) is made prominent on the homepage and across all modules with exactly one primary action per screen.\n- **Predictable Minimal Navigation**: \n  - Left: Clean single-wordmark branding (`NEXORA`).\n  - Center: Three core tabs (`Opportunities`, `Prepare`, `Progress`).\n  - Right: Quick `+ Paste Notice` CTA and live Student Profile toggle (`Aman \302\267 7.8 CGPA`), with a responsive mobile drawer.\n- **Hero Hierarchy**: Re-anchored to answer WHAT, WHO, and WHY in under 5 seconds with the primary CTA `Find my matches` and the monolithic obsidian live evaluation preview.\n- **Scannable Opportunity Feed & Job Cards**:\n  - Exact requested visual hierarchy: Company \342\206\222 Job Title \342\206\222 Circular Match Ring \342\206\222 Unambiguous Eligibility status \342\206\222 Deadline countdown \342\206\222 Important requirements \342\206\222 Action triggers.\n  - Skeletons for loading and structured empty states with clear next steps.\n- **Unambiguous Match Score & Eligibility**:\n  - SVG circular match ring with hover/tap rationale (*\"Based on your CGPA, branch, skills and job requirements\"*).\n  - Explicit badges (`\342\234\223 Eligible`, `\342\232\240 Borderline`, `\342\234\225 Not eligible`) with instant inline cutoffs (e.g., *\"Minimum CGPA: 8.5 \302\267 Your CGPA: 7.8\"*).\n- **Placement Notice Inbox**:\n  - Large comfortable input for WhatsApp/TPO circulars, 1-click sample notices (Microsoft, Razorpay, Google), multi-step progress indicator (*Reading notice... \342\206\222 Finding requirements... \342\206\222 Checking eligibility... \342\206\222 Building your match...*), and clean structured preview before saving.\n- **Personalized Resume Grill**:\n  - Focused interview preparation tool: Target Job \342\206\222 Resume Details \342\206\222 **3 Biggest Gaps** (vague metrics, async depth, testing) \342\206\222 **Questions an interviewer is likely to ask you** with technical rationales, key points to cover, and interactive practice drafts.\n- **Supportive Progress & Rejection Autopsy**:\n  - Simple 4-metric tracker: Applications (14), Interviews (4), Offers (1), Rejections (5).\n  - Constructive Rejection Autopsy: *\"YOUR BIGGEST PATTERN: 3 of your last 4 rejections happened during aptitude\"* with *\"WHAT TO DO NEXT\"* action steps and past interview takeaways.\n- **Subtle Micro-Interactions**: Smooth cursor-following glow, card hover lift, button press feedback, and dynamic live eligibility recalculation when adjusting student profile data."
    thinking: "**Verifying Initial Results**\n\nI\'ve confirmed that the initial compilation steps, including `tsc --noEmit` and `compile_applet`, have executed without reporting any errors. Now, I\'m meticulously reviewing the requirements from the user request, ensuring each element is addressed. The goal of simplifying the user journey, specifically focusing on a 5-second Nexora understanding for new students and the \"Discover opportunity\" journey, is under immediate focus.\n\n\n**Refining Website Navigation**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the website\'s navigation. I\'ve streamlined the flow to ensure it\'s intuitive throughout, integrating a clear six-step \"JourneyFlow\" right below the hero section with related headers in each module, creating a single, clear primary action for every screen, such as \"Find my matches,\" \"View opportunity,\" or \"Prepare in Grill.\" Navigation has been simplified to Opportunities, Prepare, and Progress. I\'ve also added Student context on the right side. The active page is visually obvious. I will maintain the current hero. The information hierarchy has been updated to reflect WHAT, WHO, and WHY.\n\n\n**Optimizing Opportunity Display**\n\nI\'m currently focusing on the opportunity feed and match score presentation. My aim is to create an extremely easy-to-scan, clear interface. I\'ve ensured a precise information hierarchy on each job card, starting with the company, descending to job title, match percentage, eligibility, deadline, and key requirements, finishing with a clear primary action. The match score is presented as a circular progress ring, and a concise explanation is available on hover. I\'m also ensuring eligibility is communicated using clear visual cues and precise explanations when ineligibility exists. I\'ve started focusing on the placement inbox.\n\n\n**Developing New Features**\n\nI\'m now implementing the \"Save Opportunity\" button and sample notice chips for instant usability. I\'ve outlined the Resume Grill flow: job selection, resume upload, gap identification, and interview question practice. I\'m prioritizing the presentation of the three most significant gaps with severity and recommendations. Interview questions are categorized with rationales, key points, drafts, and master toggles. I\'ve also conceived a Rejection Autopsy section for constructive feedback and a progress page with key metrics and actionable next steps.\n\n\n**Implementing Interactional Elements**\n\nI\'m now integrating crucial microcopy, prioritizing clean, approachable language tailored for Indian college students. I\'m focusing on crafting copy like \"Find jobs you actually qualify for\" and \"Learn from the rejection,\" ditching generic buzzwords. Skeleton loaders are implemented for the opportunity feeds. I\'m also progressively displaying text during AI processes: \"Reading notice...\", \"Finding requirements...\" to improve user feedback. I\'m also working on empty and error states, aiming to clearly explain *what* happened and suggest *what* to do next or how to fix it. Finally, I\'m ensuring responsive design, mobile-first tested, and working on accessibility features for high contrast, and keyboard navigation.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "The UX and UI refinement pass for **Nexora** is complete, adhering to the lavender, black, and purple editorial identity:\n\n### What was refined\n\n- **Simplified User Journey**: The 6-stage campus placement loop (*Discover Opportunity \342\206\222 Check Eligibility \342\206\222 Prepare \342\206\222 Apply \342\206\222 Track Result \342\206\222 Learn from Rejection*) is made prominent on the homepage and across all modules with exactly one primary action per screen.\n- **Predictable Minimal Navigation**: \n  - Left: Clean single-wordmark branding (`NEXORA`).\n  - Center: Three core tabs (`Opportunities`, `Prepare`, `Progress`).\n  - Right: Quick `+ Paste Notice` CTA and live Student Profile toggle (`Aman \302\267 7.8 CGPA`), with a responsive mobile drawer.\n- **Hero Hierarchy**: Re-anchored to answer WHAT, WHO, and WHY in under 5 seconds with the primary CTA `Find my matches` and the monolithic obsidian live evaluation preview.\n- **Scannable Opportunity Feed & Job Cards**:\n  - Exact requested visual hierarchy: Company \342\206\222 Job Title \342\206\222 Circular Match Ring \342\206\222 Unambiguous Eligibility status \342\206\222 Deadline countdown \342\206\222 Important requirements \342\206\222 Action triggers.\n  - Skeletons for loading and structured empty states with clear next steps.\n- **Unambiguous Match Score & Eligibility**:\n  - SVG circular match ring with hover/tap rationale (*\"Based on your CGPA, branch, skills and job requirements\"*).\n  - Explicit badges (`\342\234\223 Eligible`, `\342\232\240 Borderline`, `\342\234\225 Not eligible`) with instant inline cutoffs (e.g., *\"Minimum CGPA: 8.5 \302\267 Your CGPA: 7.8\"*).\n- **Placement Notice Inbox**:\n  - Large comfortable input for WhatsApp/TPO circulars, 1-click sample notices (Microsoft, Razorpay, Google), multi-step progress indicator (*Reading notice... \342\206\222 Finding requirements... \342\206\222 Checking eligibility... \342\206\222 Building your match...*), and clean structured preview before saving.\n- **Personalized Resume Grill**:\n  - Focused interview preparation tool: Target Job \342\206\222 Resume Details \342\206\222 **3 Biggest Gaps** (vague metrics, async depth, testing) \342\206\222 **Questions an interviewer is likely to ask you** with technical rationales, key points to cover, and interactive practice drafts.\n- **Supportive Progress & Rejection Autopsy**:\n  - Simple 4-metric tracker: Applications (14), Interviews (4), Offers (1), Rejections (5).\n  - Constructive Rejection Autopsy: *\"YOUR BIGGEST PATTERN: 3 of your last 4 rejections happened during aptitude\"* with *\"WHAT TO DO NEXT\"* action steps and past interview takeaways.\n- **Subtle Micro-Interactions**: Smooth cursor-following glow, card hover lift, button press feedback, and dynamic live eligibility recalculation when adjusting student profile data."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 8
      nanos: 525560014
    }
