  user_input {
    user_response: "Change the question system to MCQ format.\nInstead of open-ended questions, every practice/interview question must have 4 options (A, B, C, D) with only one correct answer.\n\nAfter the user selects an option:\n\nImmediately show Correct / Incorrect\nShow the correct answer\nGive a 1\342\200\2232 line explanation\nTrack the score, e.g. 7/10\nAt the end, show accuracy percentage and the topics where the user made mistakes.\n\nQuestions should be generated based on the selected company, job role, JD, and the user\'s resume/projects.\n\nKeep the UI simple, premium, and consistent with the existing Nexora design. Do not add unnecessary features or redesign the page.Use this updated prompt:\n\nAdd a dedicated \342\200\234Search Companies\342\200\235 page.\n\nUsers should be able to:\n\nSearch any company by name.\nSee available roles/openings for that company.\nSelect a specific role/job.\nImmediately see Eligible / Borderline / Not Eligible based on the student\'s saved profile (CGPA, branch, backlogs, skills, etc.).\nClearly show why they are or are not eligible.\nShow important details like salary, location, deadline, required skills, and selection process.\nProvide a clear \342\200\234Prepare for this role\342\200\235 button.\n\nImportant: Do NOT make the user paste a placement notice first just to know eligibility. Eligibility should be available directly from the Company Search page.\n\nKeep the existing Nexora design and do not add unnecessary features.\n\nMCQ Preparation: All preparation questions must use 4-option MCQs (A/B/C/D) with one correct answer, instant feedback, explanation, score, and accuracy tracking. Questions should be tailored to the selected company, role, JD, and resume/projects."
    items {
      text: "Change the question system to MCQ format.\nInstead of open-ended questions, every practice/interview question must have 4 options (A, B, C, D) with only one correct answer.\n\nAfter the user selects an option:\n\nImmediately show Correct / Incorrect\nShow the correct answer\nGive a 1\342\200\2232 line explanation\nTrack the score, e.g. 7/10\nAt the end, show accuracy percentage and the topics where the user made mistakes.\n\nQuestions should be generated based on the selected company, job role, JD, and the user\'s resume/projects.\n\nKeep the UI simple, premium, and consistent with the existing Nexora design. Do not add unnecessary features or redesign the page.Use this updated prompt:\n\nAdd a dedicated \342\200\234Search Companies\342\200\235 page.\n\nUsers should be able to:\n\nSearch any company by name.\nSee available roles/openings for that company.\nSelect a specific role/job.\nImmediately see Eligible / Borderline / Not Eligible based on the student\'s saved profile (CGPA, branch, backlogs, skills, etc.).\nClearly show why they are or are not eligible.\nShow important details like salary, location, deadline, required skills, and selection process.\nProvide a clear \342\200\234Prepare for this role\342\200\235 button.\n\nImportant: Do NOT make the user paste a placement notice first just to know eligibility. Eligibility should be available directly from the Company Search page.\n\nKeep the existing Nexora design and do not add unnecessary features.\n\nMCQ Preparation: All preparation questions must use 4-option MCQs (A/B/C/D) with one correct answer, instant feedback, explanation, score, and accuracy tracking. Questions should be tailored to the selected company, role, JD, and resume/projects."
    }
  }
}
