  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Requirement**\n\nI\'m currently dissecting the new user request. The main thrust is a shift to an MCQ format for all practice questions within the system. This means transitioning away from open-ended questions and incorporating a 4-option multiple-choice structure for every practice and interview query. I\'m focusing on the implications of this change.\n\n\n**Refining the MCQ Structure**\n\nI\'m now detailing the mechanics of the MCQ implementation. The system will provide immediate feedback (\"Correct/Incorrect\") along with the right answer and a brief explanation. Score tracking (X/Y) is essential, with a final accuracy percentage and a list of missed topics. Questions will be personalized based on the user\'s profile and target company, role, and job description.\n\n\n**Defining Role Eligibility**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the company search feature. My thinking centers on displaying clear role eligibility based on a user\'s profile data. I\'ll need to clearly show why a user is eligible, borderline, or not eligible, avoiding the need for them to paste a placement notice. Salary, location, deadlines, and required skills are all critical. A \"Prepare for this role\" button will directly link to the MCQ interview drill. I want to ensure we maintain the Nexora design system.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_266343"
      name: "view_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"AbsolutePath\":\"/src/types.ts\", \"toolAction\":\"Viewing types.ts\", \"toolSummary\":\"Check existing types\"}"
