  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Revising Question Style**\n\nI\'m currently focused on transitioning the question format to a multiple-choice structure, as requested. I\'ve just revisited the prompt to ensure complete understanding of the requirements for the format shift. My next step will be to design the necessary code modifications.\n\n\n**Implementing Question Mechanics**\n\nI\'m now integrating the feedback system for multiple-choice questions. I will immediately provide feedback as \"Correct/Incorrect\" after an option is selected. I am also implementing the explanation display, score tracking, accuracy percentage calculations, and the identification of error topics. I am also looking at the requirements of the search companies function.\n\n\n**Designing Company Listings**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the data structure for company listings and preparation. I will design the MCQ bank and company listings in `src/data/mockData.ts`. I will create a comprehensive `CompanyListing` database with top recruiting companies. Each listing will have specific roles, along with details like salary, location, deadline, required skills, selection rounds, and explicit eligibility criteria. I\'ll include a clear \"Prepare for this role\" button on each listing.\n\n\n**Generating Tailored MCQs**\n\nI am now delving into the creation of company-specific `InterviewMCQ` sets. I am focused on tailoring questions to match a candidate\'s projects/resume with each company\'s specific job description and selection process. I will be crafting detailed question banks for companies like Microsoft, Razorpay, Google, Atlassian, and PhonePe, focusing on their distinct tech stacks and interview requirements. The goal is a dynamic generator for any new role!\n\n\n**Defining Question Structures**\n\nMy current focus is on structuring each multiple-choice question. Each entry will encompass a realistic technical problem, identified by a topic, four distinct options, a designated correct answer, and a concise explanation. Additionally, a clear connection will be drawn between the question and the candidate\'s resume, in relation to the company\'s job requirements. I am incorporating these elements to improve question quality.\n\n\n**Finalizing Drill Feedback**\n\nI\'m now implementing the final feedback features for the drill. Incorrect answers will be flagged with a red cross, with the explanation displayed immediately. The score updates live, and a \"Next question\" button will appear. Upon completion, a summary card will show the final score, accuracy percentage, and tone (like \"Ready for Day 0\"). It will also list error topics with guidance and offer options to retry, review, or select another company.\n\n\n"
