  planner_response {
    response: "### What was implemented\n\n1. **4-Option MCQ Interview Drill System (Resume Grill)**:\n   - Replaced open-ended responses with 4-option MCQs (`A`, `B`, `C`, `D`) with a single correct answer.\n   - Questions are tailored to the selected company, role, JD, and the student\'s resume tech stack (FastAPI, Python, React, SQL, and DSA).\n   - **Instant Feedback**: Clicking an option reveals whether it was correct or incorrect, highlights the true correct answer in green, and provides a 1\342\200\2232 line technical explanation.\n   - **Live Score Tracking**: Tracks live score (e.g. `Score: 3 / 5`) throughout the drill.\n   - **Summary & Topic Breakdown**: Displays final score, accuracy percentage, and a dedicated breakdown of the specific topics where mistakes occurred with key takeaways.\n\n2. **Dedicated \342\200\234Search Companies\342\200\235 Page**:\n   - Added `Companies` to the top navigation and 6-step campus placement loop.\n   - **Instant Search**: Search recruiting companies by name (Microsoft, Razorpay, Google, Amazon, Atlassian, PhonePe, Morgan Stanley, etc.) with category filters.\n   - **Immediate Eligibility Verification**: Without pasting any notices, the page evaluates eligibility directly against the student\'s saved profile (CGPA, branch, backlogs) with clear reasons (e.g. *\"Your CGPA (7.8) clears the 7.5 minimum cutoff\"* or *\"Minimum CGPA: 8.5 \302\267 Your CGPA: 7.8\"*).\n   - **Role Details**: Shows salary (CTC), location, deadline countdown, required skills, and selection rounds for each opening.\n   - **Action Trigger**: Includes a `Prepare for this role` button that launches the MCQ interview drill for that role."
    thinking: "**Verifying Instruction Compliance**\n\nI\'m pleased to report that the initial build and lint steps completed flawlessly, without a hitch. Now, I\'m meticulously re-examining the user\'s instructions to confirm that every requirement has been addressed comprehensively.\n\n\n**Refining User Interaction**\n\nI\'ve successfully integrated the immediate feedback mechanism. This includes highlighting the correct answer and providing explanations upon user selection. Furthermore, I am now dynamically displaying the running score and accuracy, updating live as the user progresses through the questions.\n\n\n**Analyzing Company Profiles**\n\nI\'ve integrated the detailed company and role search feature. Now, I can immediately assess a user\'s eligibility for specific positions, factoring in their profile details like CGPA, skills, and backlogs. I clearly display the eligibility status with justifications. Also, the roles display important details, such as salary, location, deadline, required skills, and the selection process. I\'m focusing on ensuring accurate and insightful insights.\n\n\n"
