      metadata_index: 53
      cascade_id: "4f5f1ea5-ea03-4d06-97b4-99b1cf9d6906"
    }
  }
  user_input {
    user_response: "Make the following changes to the existing Nexora website without redesigning the overall visual style.\n\n1. Remove Placement Notice Extractor\n\nCompletely remove the Placement Notice / Notice Extractor feature from the navigation, homepage, dashboard, buttons, and related UI.\nRemove its cards, upload/paste notice interface, and any unused references.\n\n2. Make \342\200\234Applications\342\200\235 highly clickable\n\nTurn the Applications section/card into a clear interactive element.\nClicking it should open an Applications page showing all applications with statuses such as:\nApplied\nIn Progress\nInterview\nRejected\nSelected\nUse clear clickable cards/rows with hover and active states.\n\n3. Make \342\200\234Rejected Applications\342\200\235 clickable\n\nThe Rejected count/card must be clickable.\nClicking it opens a Rejection Analysis / Rejection Autopsy page showing the user\'s rejected applications.\nEach rejection should be clickable to view the company, role, rejection stage, and reason/pattern.\n\n4. Make \342\200\234Interview Offers\342\200\235 clickable\n\nThe Interview / Interview Offers section must be fully clickable.\nClicking it opens a page showing upcoming interviews and interview-related applications.\nEach interview card should be clickable to view company, role, date, stage, and preparation status.\n\n5. Make dashboard statistics interactive\n\nAny cards showing Applications, Interviews, Rejections, Offers/Selections should behave like navigation cards.\nAdd subtle hover animation, cursor feedback, and a clear clickable visual state.\nNever make a card look clickable unless it actually navigates somewhere.\n\n6. Keep the current design\n\nPreserve the existing Nexora lavender, deep-purple, black visual identity.\nDo not redesign the homepage.\nDo not add unnecessary features.\nFocus only on making the existing sections functional, connected, and clearly clickable."
    items {
      text: "Make the following changes to the existing Nexora website without redesigning the overall visual style.\n\n1. Remove Placement Notice Extractor\n\nCompletely remove the Placement Notice / Notice Extractor feature from the navigation, homepage, dashboard, buttons, and related UI.\nRemove its cards, upload/paste notice interface, and any unused references.\n\n2. Make \342\200\234Applications\342\200\235 highly clickable\n\nTurn the Applications section/card into a clear interactive element.\nClicking it should open an Applications page showing all applications with statuses such as:\nApplied\nIn Progress\nInterview\nRejected\nSelected\nUse clear clickable cards/rows with hover and active states.\n\n3. Make \342\200\234Rejected Applications\342\200\235 clickable\n\nThe Rejected count/card must be clickable.\nClicking it opens a Rejection Analysis / Rejection Autopsy page showing the user\'s rejected applications.\nEach rejection should be clickable to view the company, role, rejection stage, and reason/pattern.\n\n4. Make \342\200\234Interview Offers\342\200\235 clickable\n\nThe Interview / Interview Offers section must be fully clickable.\nClicking it opens a page showing upcoming interviews and interview-related applications.\nEach interview card should be clickable to view company, role, date, stage, and preparation status.\n\n5. Make dashboard statistics interactive\n\nAny cards showing Applications, Interviews, Rejections, Offers/Selections should behave like navigation cards.\nAdd subtle hover animation, cursor feedback, and a clear clickable visual state.\nNever make a card look clickable unless it actually navigates somewhere.\n\n6. Keep the current design\n\nPreserve the existing Nexora lavender, deep-purple, black visual identity.\nDo not redesign the homepage.\nDo not add unnecessary features.\nFocus only on making the existing sections functional, connected, and clearly clickable."
    }
  }
}
