  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Application Types**\n\nI\'m working on defining a rich `ApplicationRecord` type. I\'ve begun to flesh out the core structure, focusing on key properties. I\'ve also identified a set of statuses to use. I\'m aiming to create a solid foundation for representing the application data. Currently, I\'m thinking of \"Applied\", \"In Progress\", \"Interview\", \"Rejected\" and \"Selected\".\n\n\n**Refining Application Properties**\n\nI\'m now diving deeper into the `ApplicationRecord` type. I\'ve added more detailed properties to it, including `role`, `ctc`, `location`, `appliedDate`, and fields for rejection reasons and interview details. My thought is that it is crucial to capture specific data, allowing for richer filtering and analysis. Now I\'m focused on populating `mockData.ts` with records to test the structure. I\'m aiming for realistic application scenarios, including those for Aman Sharma.\n\n\n**Tracking Application Lifecycle**\n\nI\'m now tracking the lifecycle of my applications. I\'ve noted down interview schedules for Razorpay, Microsoft, PhonePe, and Atlassian. I\'m also cataloging those \"In Progress\" or \"Applied\" at companies like Amazon, Google, Morgan Stanley, and Swiggy. Rejections, unfortunately, are stacking up too; I\'m logging those as well from companies such as Swiggy, Amazon, CRED, TCS Digital, and Meesho. I now have a comprehensive view with a total of fourteen applications. Also, I\'m removing the \"Paste Notice\" functionality from the application.\n\n\n**Refactoring Application Interface**\n\nI\'m now refactoring the user interface to align with an application-centric focus. I\'m removing the \"Paste Notice\" functionality from the homepage, opportunity feed, journey flow, and footer, and deleting the associated modal. The applications section will become a highly clickable element, opening a dedicated applications page with clear cards or rows, displaying statuses like \"Applied,\" \"In Progress,\" and more with interactive hover and active states.\n\n\n**Enhancing User Interactions**\n\nNow, I\'m making the dashboard statistics interactive. The application counters, such as \"All,\" \"Applied,\" \"Interview,\" \"Selected/Offer,\" and \"Rejected,\" are now clickable to reveal filtered lists. Clicking each application opens a detailed timeline, stage info, notes, and a \"Prepare in Grill\" button. I\'ve also made the \"Rejected Applications\" and \"Interview Offers\" sections clickable, linking them to their corresponding analysis pages with detailed data.\n\n\n**Structuring Application Views**\n\nI\'ve made the application counter cards on the dashboard clickable. Each now opens a dedicated view. The \"All Applications\" card displays a list of all applications, \"Interviews\" shows upcoming ones, \"Offers\" displays offer letters, and \"Rejections\" opens a rejection autopsy. I\'ve added hover animations and visual cues, such as \"View all...\" labels. I am focusing on making sure all clickable elements navigate to relevant views. I\'m reviewing navigation options, focusing on structure for a smoother user experience.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_517107"
      name: "view_file"
