    thinking: "**Defining Mock Data Structure**\n\nI\'ve just updated `src/data/mockData.ts`. I imported `ApplicationRecord` from `../types`. I removed `sampleNotices` and added `initialApplications: ApplicationRecord[]`. It contains all 14 applications with full details, spanning Applied, In Progress, Interview, Rejected, and Selected states. Now, I\'m thinking about how the new structure impacts application retrieval.\n\n\n**Updating Application States**\n\nI\'ve just added the application states to my thought process. I have successfully added the following: Oracle - Selected, Razorpay - Interview, Microsoft - Interview, PhonePe - Interview, Atlassian - Interview, Amazon - In Progress, Google - In Progress, Morgan Stanley - Applied, and Flipkart - Applied. I need to make sure to update these states as the application progresses.\n\n\n**Adding Rejection Reasons**\n\nI\'ve just added rejection reasons for five more applications. Specifically, I\'ve logged the reasons for rejection for the following applications: 1 (\342\202\27116 LPA), Amazon \342\200\224 SDE Intern (\342\202\27180,000 / mo), CRED \342\200\224 Frontend Engineer Intern (\342\202\2711,00,000 / mo), TCS Digital \342\200\224 Systems Engineer (\342\202\2719 LPA), and Meesho \342\200\224 Software Engineer (\342\202\27120 LPA). I\'ve noted the stage and the key reason for the rejections, such as aptitude test speed or failing on React internals or concurrency issues. The application statistics still match perfectly!\n\n\n"
