  planner_response {
    response: "The requested updates have been implemented without altering Nexora\'s visual identity:\n\n### 1. Completely Removed Placement Notice Extractor\n- Removed the **Paste Notice** and **Notice Extractor** buttons and interfaces from the navigation bar, mobile menu, hero section, opportunity feed, and footer.\n- Deleted `PlacementInboxModal.tsx` and removed all unused state and references.\n- Updated Step 01 of the 6-step loop to *\"Discover: Browse verified campus openings\"*.\n\n### 2. Highly Interactive Applications View\n- The **Applications (14)** statistic card now features interactive hover states and cursor feedback.\n- Clicking it opens the **All Applications** view, displaying all 14 campus applications with real-time status filters:\n  - `Applied` (2)\n  - `In Progress` (2)\n  - `Interview` (4)\n  - `Selected` (1)\n  - `Rejected` (5)\n- Each application row is an interactive card that opens a detailed sheet with company info, package, current stage, timeline, and a direct `Prepare in Grill` action.\n\n### 3. Clickable Rejections & Diagnostic Autopsy\n- The **Rejections (5)** statistic card is fully clickable.\n- Clicking it opens the **Rejection Autopsy** view with the emotional diagnostic pattern (*\"3 of your last 4 rejections happened during aptitude\"*).\n- Every rejected drive (Swiggy, Amazon, CRED, TCS Digital, Meesho) is clickable to inspect the exact failure stage, root bottleneck, and actionable lesson learned.\n\n### 4. Clickable Interviews & Offers\n- The **Interviews (4)** and **Offers (1)** statistic cards are fully clickable.\n- Clicking **Interviews** opens the scheduled rounds with interview dates, stage details, preparation focus, and a 1-click trigger to start the role-specific MCQ drill in Resume Grill.\n- Clicking **Offers** displays confirmed campus placement letters (e.g. Oracle, \342\202\27114 LPA).\n\n### 5. Interactive Dashboard Statistics\n- All metric cards on the dashboard (`Applications`, `Interviews`, `Offers`, `Rejections`) now serve as navigation cards with hover lift animations, cursor pointers, and clear visual indicators that transition between views."
    thinking: "**Verifying User Request**\n\nI\'ve confirmed that the `compile_applet` and `lint_applet` commands executed without errors. I\'m now cross-referencing all aspects of the user\'s request. Specifically, I\'ve completely removed the `PlacementNotice` and `NoticeExtractor` components from the specified files, including the Navigation bar, where I\'ve removed the \"+ Paste Notice\" text.\n\n\n**Refining Interface Elements**\n\nI\'ve just refined several interface elements. The \"Applications\" card on the `ProgressPage` is now a prominent, highly clickable navigation point, complete with hover effects and an \"Open \342\206\222\" indicator. This directly links to a full application view, showing all applications across statuses, and incorporating filter buttons for easy access. I\'ve completely removed the \"Paste a college notice\" button, and text, from the desktop and mobile menus.\n\n\n**Enhancing Dashboard Statistics**\n\nI\'m now making the dashboard statistics interactive, focusing on improved user engagement. Specifically, I\'ve made the \"Rejected Applications\" and \"Interview Offers\" metrics clickable. The Rejections card now leads to a Rejection Autopsy view, detailing rejected applications. The Interview Offers card opens an Interviews & Offers view, showing upcoming interviews with prep focus. Each card includes a direct action button, linking to \"Prepare in Grill\".\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "The requested updates have been implemented without altering Nexora\'s visual identity:\n\n### 1. Completely Removed Placement Notice Extractor\n- Removed the **Paste Notice** and **Notice Extractor** buttons and interfaces from the navigation bar, mobile menu, hero section, opportunity feed, and footer.\n- Deleted `PlacementInboxModal.tsx` and removed all unused state and references.\n- Updated Step 01 of the 6-step loop to *\"Discover: Browse verified campus openings\"*.\n\n### 2. Highly Interactive Applications View\n- The **Applications (14)** statistic card now features interactive hover states and cursor feedback.\n- Clicking it opens the **All Applications** view, displaying all 14 campus applications with real-time status filters:\n  - `Applied` (2)\n  - `In Progress` (2)\n  - `Interview` (4)\n  - `Selected` (1)\n  - `Rejected` (5)\n- Each application row is an interactive card that opens a detailed sheet with company info, package, current stage, timeline, and a direct `Prepare in Grill` action.\n\n### 3. Clickable Rejections & Diagnostic Autopsy\n- The **Rejections (5)** statistic card is fully clickable.\n- Clicking it opens the **Rejection Autopsy** view with the emotional diagnostic pattern (*\"3 of your last 4 rejections happened during aptitude\"*).\n- Every rejected drive (Swiggy, Amazon, CRED, TCS Digital, Meesho) is clickable to inspect the exact failure stage, root bottleneck, and actionable lesson learned.\n\n### 4. Clickable Interviews & Offers\n- The **Interviews (4)** and **Offers (1)** statistic cards are fully clickable.\n- Clicking **Interviews** opens the scheduled rounds with interview dates, stage details, preparation focus, and a 1-click trigger to start the role-specific MCQ drill in Resume Grill.\n- Clicking **Offers** displays confirmed campus placement letters (e.g. Oracle, \342\202\27114 LPA).\n\n### 5. Interactive Dashboard Statistics\n- All metric cards on the dashboard (`Applications`, `Interviews`, `Offers`, `Rejections`) now serve as navigation cards with hover lift animations, cursor pointers, and clear visual indicators that transition between views."
